WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.811 --> 00:00:11.973
Once upon a time, there was an old woman who longed to make an apple pie.

2
00:00:12.813 --> 00:00:18.396
She had plenty of flour, butter, sugar, and cinnamon, but she didn't have any apples.

3
00:00:20.117 --> 00:00:22.318
All she had was a tree full of plums.

4
00:00:23.558 --> 00:00:27.220
The more the woman thought about that apple pie, the more she craved it.

5
00:00:28.732 --> 00:00:32.273
So one day she filled a basket with her plums and headed down the road.

6
00:00:32.293 --> 00:00:37.695
"I will find someone who will trade me some apples for my plums!"

7
00:00:38.235 --> 00:00:38.635
she said.

8
00:00:39.315 --> 00:00:43.636
The old woman had walked only a short distance when she spotted a young woman in a yard.

9
00:00:44.436 --> 00:00:46.297
Perhaps this young woman would barter with her.

10
00:00:47.437 --> 00:00:49.178
The old woman called to the young woman.

11
00:00:49.198 --> 00:00:51.018
"Excuse me.

12
00:00:51.038 --> 00:00:53.159
Do you have any apples?

13
00:00:53.739 --> 00:00:56.600
My heart is set on making an apple pie.

14
00:00:57.224 --> 00:01:01.946
I will give you my whole basket of plums in exchange for some apples."

15
00:01:03.266 --> 00:01:04.506
The young woman shook her head.

16
00:01:04.526 --> 00:01:08.468
"I don't have any apples," she said regretfully.

17
00:01:08.488 --> 00:01:12.669
"However, my husband adores plum jelly with his cooked goose.

18
00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:17.030
"Will you take a bag of feathers in exchange for your plums?"

19
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:22.952
"One pleased is better than two disappointed," the old woman declared.

20
00:01:24.004 --> 00:01:26.845
Soon the old woman had exchanged her plums for the feathers.

21
00:01:27.626 --> 00:01:33.388
Then she walked down a hill and came upon a garden bursting with beautiful lilies, lilacs, and roses.

22
00:01:34.128 --> 00:01:36.809
The old woman paused at the gate to admire the flowers.

23
00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:41.091
Nearby she heard a man and a woman arguing loudly.

24
00:01:41.111 --> 00:01:43.932
"Cotton!" said the woman.

25
00:01:43.952 --> 00:01:46.654
"Straw!" insisted the man.

26
00:01:47.494 --> 00:01:51.075
The couple continued arguing until the woman finally spotted the visitor.

27
00:01:51.095 --> 00:01:53.933
"Look," the woman said to her husband.

28
00:01:53.953 --> 00:01:56.736
"There is an old woman at our gate.

29
00:01:57.136 --> 00:01:59.158
Perhaps she can settle our dispute."

30
00:01:59.178 --> 00:02:01.841
"It's worth a try," he agreed.

31
00:02:01.861 --> 00:02:06.225
"Excuse me," the wife called to the old woman.

32
00:02:06.245 --> 00:02:15.373
"If you were making a pillow for your grandfather's bed, would you stuff it with cotton or straw?"

33
00:02:15.393 --> 00:02:17.896
"Neither," the old woman responded briskly.

34
00:02:18.796 --> 00:02:20.437
"I would stuff it with feathers.

35
00:02:21.018 --> 00:02:24.580
A feather pillow is fit for a king," she continued.

36
00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:30.604
"In fact, I have a bag of feathers that I would happily trade for some apples."

37
00:02:31.545 --> 00:02:33.526
The husband and wife exchanged glances.

38
00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:38.009
They had no apples, but perhaps they could offer the old woman something else.

39
00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:43.873
Soon, with a bouquet of lovely flowers in her basket, the old woman was on her way again.

40
00:02:44.914 --> 00:02:47.996
After traveling for a while, she encountered a handsome lord.

41
00:02:48.492 --> 00:02:50.254
The young man seemed full of despair.

42
00:02:50.274 --> 00:02:56.239
"My lord," inquired the old woman, "why do you look so sad?"

43
00:02:56.259 --> 00:03:00.482
"I promised to meet my lady," he replied solemnly.

44
00:03:00.502 --> 00:03:03.505
"But I have forgotten the ring I intended to give her.

45
00:03:04.325 --> 00:03:06.727
Now I must go to my love empty-handed."

46
00:03:08.229 --> 00:03:12.072
"You shall have a gift for your lady," the old woman declared.

47
00:03:12.924 --> 00:03:19.369
"I was hoping to barter these flowers for some apples, but love is certainly more delicious than an

48
00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.330
apple pie."

49
00:03:22.192 --> 00:03:25.054
With a flourish, she presented the bouquet to the young lord.

50
00:03:25.575 --> 00:03:27.256
The lord's face instantly brightened.

51
00:03:27.276 --> 00:03:28.757
"Thank you!"

52
00:03:29.137 --> 00:03:31.519
he said to the old woman, overcome with gratitude.

53
00:03:31.539 --> 00:03:36.564
"However, I cannot accept such a beautiful gift without giving you something in return.

54
00:03:37.164 --> 00:03:39.106
Here, please take my gold chain."

55
00:03:40.026 --> 00:03:41.708
It was the woman's turn to be delighted.

56
00:03:42.428 --> 00:03:49.591
"With this precious gold chain, I can buy all the apples in the king's market, and still have

57
00:03:49.631 --> 00:03:50.912
some money left over!"

58
00:03:51.412 --> 00:03:51.812
she thought.

59
00:03:52.973 --> 00:03:55.514
She hurried to town as fast as her feet could carry her.

60
00:03:56.615 --> 00:04:00.676
She had almost arrived at the market when she noticed a poor mother huddled with her children.

61
00:04:00.696 --> 00:04:04.758
"My children are starving," the mother murmured.

62
00:04:04.778 --> 00:04:08.320
"We have no food, and I have no money."

63
00:04:09.684 --> 00:04:12.686
The old woman glimpsed the precious gold chain in her basket.

64
00:04:13.727 --> 00:04:20.411
"Never shall someone say that I made apple pie for dinner and let my neighbor starve," she said

65
00:04:20.471 --> 00:04:24.254
softly. Slowly, she reached into the basket for the chain.

66
00:04:27.616 --> 00:04:30.198
The old woman headed for home with her empty basket.

67
00:04:30.958 --> 00:04:34.901
She had not walked very far when the poor mother and her children chased after her.

68
00:04:34.921 --> 00:04:39.484
"We have only one thing to give you," said the mother.

69
00:04:40.064 --> 00:04:41.445
"Please take this puppy.

70
00:04:42.205 --> 00:04:45.147
His love will be a reminder of our appreciation."

71
00:04:45.927 --> 00:04:49.830
The old woman thanked the family, and then gently placed the puppy in the basket.

72
00:04:52.271 --> 00:04:56.833
As she turned a corner, she saw a tall tree—laden with ripe, juicy apples!

73
00:04:57.774 --> 00:04:59.195
Nearby stood an old man.

74
00:04:59.215 --> 00:05:05.919
"That's a fine tree of apples," the old woman called to him.

75
00:05:06.899 --> 00:05:08.240
The man nodded and looked away.

76
00:05:09.088 --> 00:05:12.510
"Yes, it's a fine tree, but I have no one to share it with.

77
00:05:13.331 --> 00:05:17.274
My wife died years ago, and all of my children live far away."

78
00:05:18.475 --> 00:05:21.597
Just then the puppy barked and poked his head out of the basket.

79
00:05:22.557 --> 00:05:24.979
The lonely old man beamed at the sight of the puppy.

80
00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:27.341
The old woman smiled too.

81
00:05:28.241 --> 00:05:30.103
A wonderful idea had occurred to her.

82
00:05:31.023 --> 00:05:33.685
Soon the old woman was walking toward home again.

83
00:05:34.626 --> 00:05:37.508
At last her basket was filled with apples for a pie.

84
00:05:38.729 --> 00:05:47.271
"If you try long enough and hard enough," she said contentedly, "you will get some apples for plums."
